{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DateComponents\/yearForWeekOfYear","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DateComponents"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The year corresponding to a week-counting week."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DateComponents\/era","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DateComponents\/year","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DateComponents\/quarter","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DateComponents\/month","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DateComponents\/isLeapMonth"],"anchor":"Working-with-months-and-years","generated":true,"title":"Working with months and years"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"yearForWeekOfYear","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":"? { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Gregorian calendar defines a week to have 7 days, and a year to have 365 days, or 366 in a leap year. However, neither 365 or 366 divide evenly into a 7 day week, so it is often the case that the last week of a year ends on a day in the next year, and the first week of a year begins in the preceding year. To reconcile this, ISO 8601 defines a week-numbering year, consisting of either 52 or 53 full weeks (364 or 371 days), such that the first week of a year is designated to be the week containing the first Thursday of the year."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can use the yearForWeekOfYear property with the weekOfYear and weekday properties to get the date corresponding to a particular weekday of a given week of a year. For example, the 6th day of the 53rd week of the year 2005 (ISO 2005-W53-6) corresponds to Sat 1 January 2005 on the Gregorian calendar."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This value is interpreted in the context of the calendar in which it is used."}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/datecomponents\/yearforweekofyear"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"FoundationEssentials"}],"externalID":"s:20FoundationEssentials14DateComponentsV17yearForWeekOfYearSiSgvp","platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false},{"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"10.9"},{"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"9.0"},{"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"2.0"}],"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"yearForWeekOfYear","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"yearForWeekOfYear","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"te